  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Ofev (nintedanib) Criteria Version 1: Original 12/02/20; Approval 1/15/21; Effective 3/15/21.",
    "Encoded: three closed indications, shared approval criteria 1–4, indication-gated criterion 5 and denial criteria 2–3. Denial criterion 1 (failure to meet approval criteria) is represented by the approval clauses. Clinical documentation attestations require manual review.",
    "Cautions (notes only): monitor elevated ALT, AST and bilirubin and drug-induced liver injury; gastrointestinal perforation, severe diarrhea, nausea and vomiting; fetal harm and highly effective contraception for women of childbearing age; bleeding events.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization approval up to 12 months.",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): 60 × 100 mg tablets per 30 days; 60 × 150 mg tablets per 30 days. Numeric quantity enforcement is not encoded.",
    "Documentation verification, monitoring, duration, reauthorization and quantity limits require manual review. Esbriet is linked as an alternative subject to its own criteria."
  ],
